  "english": "Eleventh Sunday. [Hymn of the] Questions of the Resurrection.\nMidday Psalm 64 [65]: \"Praise is due to you\" [Kez vayel e].\nProphet Isaiah 29:11 to verse 20: \"And it shall be to you... the ruthless [wicked] to evil.\"\nEpistle of the Apostle Philippians 4:8 to verse 24 [23]: \"Finally, brethren... with your [spirit], Amen.\"\nAlleluia: Resurrection, according to the tone of the day.\nGospel according to Luke 11:1 to verse 13: \"And it came to pass in a [certain] place... ask of Him.\"\n\nBut the Feast of the Presentation of the three-year-old Holy Virgin in the Temple is placed here, which is always celebrated on November 21.\nIn the evening: perform a pre-feast [Nakhatonak].\nHymn [Sharakan], Tone 1 [ahk]: \"Who foreknew\" [Vor nakhimats], with its proper canons.\nAnd in the morning: Morning Hymn [Aravotyan Hymn], Tone 6 [gkee]: \"Sing, O children\" [Yerketsek vortik], with its proper canons.\nMorning Song: \"He shall come down like rain\" [Idjtse vorpes zantsrev].\nLitany: \"Holy Mother\" [Mayr surb].\nTrisagion [Holy God], according to the proper of the day.\nPsalm 67 [68]: \"The Lord will give the word\" [Ter tatse zban]. Antiphon: \"Let God arise\" [Haritse astvats].\nBook of Song of Songs 1:1: \"Let him kiss me... to verse 11: ...shall receive you.\"\nProverbs 11:30: \"From the fruit of righteousness... to 12:4: ...to her husband.\"\nProphet Isaiah 52:7: \"Thus says the Lord: How [beautiful]... to verse 10: ...of our God.\"\nProphet Zechariah 2:10: \"Sing and rejoice... to verse 13: ...His holy habitation [saints].\"\nProphet Malachi 3:1: \"Behold, I send... to verse 2: ...of his appearance [coming].\"\nEpistle of the Apostle 2 Corinthians 6:16: \"For you are [the temple]... to 7:1: ...in the fear of God.\"\nAlleluia: \"The Holy Spirit shall come upon you\" [Hogin surb ekestse].\nGospel according to Luke 1:39: \"Mary arose... to verse 56: ...to her house.\"\nHymn of Creation [Ararchakan], according to the proper; if it falls on a Sunday: \"Newly created\" [Norasteghtsyal].\nLitany: \"The Holy Mother of God\" [Surb zastvatsatsinn]. \"Save [us, O Lord]\" [Ketso].\nPrayer: \"Receive, O Lord\" [Enkal ter].\n\nMidday Introit [Zhamamut]: \"We confess you, Mother of God\" [Astvatsatsin zkez khostovanyal].\nHymn [Sharakan], Tone 6 [gkee]: \"Tree of life\" [Tsar kenats].\nPsalm, scripture, and gospel, according to the proper of the day.\nEucharistic Hymn [Srbasatsutyun]: \"Multitudes\" [Bazmutiunk].\nIn the Evening: Gradual [Mesedi]: \"He shall come down like rain\" [Idjtse vorpes zantsrev].\nLitany: \"Holy Mother\" [Mayr surb].\nEvening Hymn [Hambartsi], Tone 7 [dzah]: \"Born of New Zion\" [Nor sion tsnyal].\nThereafter: \"The Holy Mother of God\" [Surb zastvatsatsinn]. \"Save [us, O Lord]\" [Ketso]. Prayer: \"Receive, O Lord\" [Enkal ter].\n\nFrom here until the end, although these feasts and intervals are placed as immovable, nevertheless, some feasts occasionally move, and the interval after Saint Jacob [James] increases and decreases.\nTherefore, keep the Directory [Taregir] as your rule, and conduct yourself by it until the end of the year.\nAnd then the Fast of Advent [Yisnakats], but there are no feasts.\n\nMonday of the Fast. [Hymn of the] Questions of Repentance.\nMidday Hymn [Sharakan], Tone 5 [gtsah]: \"Remember, Christ God\" [Kristos astvats hishya].\nPsalm 144 [145]: \"Your kingdom\" [Arkayutyun].\nEpistle of the Apostle Colossians 1:1: \"Paul, an apostle... to verse 11: ...longsuffering [patience].\"\nAlleluia: \"Come, let us sing\" [Yekayk tsntsastskuk].\nGospel according to Luke 11:14: \"And he was casting out a demon... to verse 23: ...scatters.\"\n\nTuesday. [Hymn of the] Questions of Repentance.\nMidday Psalm 5: \"I will worship toward your holy temple\" [Erkirpagits i tajar surb ko].\nEpistle of the Apostle Colossians 1:12: \"Brethren, giving thanks... to verse 23: ...Paul, a minister [servant].\"\nAlleluia: \"Sing to the Lord a new song\" [Yerketsek tyarn yerg nor].\nGospel according to Luke 11:27: \"And it came to pass, as He spoke... to verse 32: ...something greater than Jonah is here.\"\n\nWednesday. [Hymn of the] Questions of Repentance.\nMidday Hymn [Sharakan], Tone 8 [dkee]: \"Glorification\" [Parabanutyun].\nPsalm 85 [86]: \"Save your servant\" [Ketso ztsarays ko].\nEpistle of the Apostle Colossians 1:24: \"And now I rejoice... to 2:7: ...with thanksgiving.\"\nAlleluia: according to the tone of the day.\nGospel according to Luke 11:33: \"No one after lighting [a lamp]... to verse 42: ...not to neglect.\"\n\nThursday. [Hymn of the] Questions of Repentance.\nMidday Psalm 98 [99]: \"Extol [the Lord]\" [Bardzr ararek].\nEpistle of the Apostle Colossians 3:15: \"Brethren, be thankful... to 4:4: ...as I ought to speak.\"\nAlleluia: \"Extol [the Lord]\" [Bardzr ararek].\nGospel according to Luke 11:49: \"For this reason... to verse 54: ...speaking evil of Him.\"\n\nFriday. [Hymn of the] Questions of Rest.\nMidday Hymn [Sharakan], Tone 8 [dkee]: \"Who out of nothing\" [Vor yaneyits].\nPsalm 97 [98]: \"All [the ends of the earth] have seen\" [Tesin amenayn].\nEpistle of the Apostle Colossians 4:5: \"Conduct yourselves with wisdom... to verse 18: ...Grace be with you.\"\nAlleluia: according to the tone of the day.\nGospel according to Luke 12:1: \"When [many thousands of the multitude] had gathered... to verse 12: ...what you ought to say.\"",
